meta {
  name: create comparison
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/comparisons
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "documentVersionId": "{{documentVersionId}}",
    "standardVersionIds": ["{{standardVersionId}}"],
    "department": "",
    "standardFamily": "",
    "documentType": "",
    "comparisonGuidance": ""
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
}

docs {
  Starts a review. WRITES — it costs model calls.

  Leave standardVersionIds EMPTY to exercise auto-selection: it picks the single best match and
  refuses if nothing clears the relevance floor.

  `documentType` is the highest-value field: without it, every scoped requirement becomes an open
  applicability question a person must answer.

  A run exceeding the requirement cap (500 by default) is rejected up front with the count, not
  silently truncated.
}
